--- stdout ---
Fixed and verified. The bug was exactly where the source suspected: `clampToStorageCap` in `src/resources/storage.ts:22` clamped wood and stone with `Math.min(…, cap)` but passed food through untouched, so every `advanceTurn` let food grow unbounded while the other two hit the storehouse cap.

What changed (all under the run root):

- `src/resources/storage.ts` — food is now clamped identically: `food: Math.min(resources.food, cap)`. Also removed the two now-stale "still-buggy food" annotations that pointed at this exact flaw.
- `tests/settlement.test.ts` — added a `clampToStorageCap` suite (food clamps to base cap, never raises under-cap resources, obeys a storehouse-raised cap) and an end-to-end `advanceTurn` test running 20 turns with 8 farms, asserting food settles exactly at the 50 cap. This one failed against the old code in an interesting way (my first draft with 3 farms ended at 24 because population growth ate the surplus — still over/under the cap unpredictably); the 8-farm version goes uncapped → capped cleanly.

Verification: `npx vitest run` → 19/19 tests pass (was 1 failing before the scenario fix), `npx tsc --noEmit` → clean. No other resource-increasing path exists — production is the only one (builds deduct, raid/drought subtract) — so food now caps the same way as everything else, and the utilization display's existing 1-clamp stays honest.


